\par\par \b \uc2  Colombia cenbank ups repo rates, peso falls again. \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, Feb 16 (Reuters) - A rise in overnight repo rates did little to stop Colombia's peso sliding further against the dollar Monday and interbank traders said they did not expect the move to have any effect until at least next week. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased overnight repo rates by three points to 30 percent late Friday -- two days after upping open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates from 21.5 percent to 23 percent. \par \par \uc2  The peso closed at a new historic low of 1,351.16 Monday -- on the floor of the daily exchange rate band. \par \par \uc2  Interbank traders said the peso has become the target of speculative attacks and that Colombian importers are snapping up greenbacks to make early payments to foreign creditors while exporters are withholding earnings in the expectation of further rises in the dollar rate. \par \par \uc2  In comments Monday, one trader, who did not wish to be named said he did not expect any recovery in the peso as a response to the repo rates rise until "next week at the earliest". He added that at best the peso would only gain "a maximum 10 pesos" against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The peso interbank rate has lost 4.45 percent in the year so far compared to the close of 1997. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has forecast a 13 percent nominal devaluation in the peso this year. \par \par \uc2  According to the National Association of Financial Institutions (ANIF), the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent $130 million propping up the peso last Thursday and Friday. \par \par \uc2  In the year so far, ANIF says reserves have fallen $388 million, largely as a result of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's net reserves stood at $9.7 billion at the close of January, the last date for which official figures are available, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  ((--Karl Penhaul, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944, bogota.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du2g03zlh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
