\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso Closes Down After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 257 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 1998\par 23:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--The embattled Colombian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened further against the U.S. dollar Friday, despite renewed resolve by the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fend off speculative attacks on the peso, brokers said. \par \par \uc2  The peso's average exchange rate rose to 1349.59 to the dollar, from 1349.36 to the dollar on Thursday. Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  once again to shore up the peso, selling roughly $26.0 million of reserves late in the day. \par \par \uc2  However, that figure was significantly lower than traders' estimates for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the week, put at around $100.0 million on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The peso gained some ground against the dollar in early trading, brokers said, boosted by a Treasury Department statement suggesting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would take new measures to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, demand for dollars rose toward the end of the session, driving the peso's value down. \par \par \uc2  'The industrial sector was looking for dollars later in the day to meet (foreign) debt obligations,' a trader said. \par \par \uc2  Friday's trading fluctuated between 1348.90 and 1349.84 pesos to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume was $202.0 million, down from $255.0 million the previous day. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the 'next day market,' which reflects trades made late one\par afternoon but not delivered until the following morning, the dollar\par traded at 1,351.40, traders said.\par -By Ruth Morris; 201-938-4381; rmorris@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 13-02-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2200GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1068 1845 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du2d018rn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
