\par\par \b \uc2  Colombia/Peso/Salomon -2:Strong Growth Way To Cut Deficit \b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 1997\par 20:30\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Also a moderate depreciation has been welcomed by economic authorities, Salomon said. With domestic demand weak and unemployment high at 13.6% in July, a weaker peso is welcomed by the government. \par \par \uc2  "Stronger growth might be the only means to reduce the increasing budget deficit," the report said. \par \par \uc2  In recent weeks, \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buttress the peso perhaps because of political pressures to reactivate the economy, Salomon said. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, however, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Despite Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , volatility remains high in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market "as there are increasing doubts about the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's willingness to prevent the peso from depreciating further, as inaction has been the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behavior in recent episodes," the report said. \par \par \uc2  On Sept. 9 the band in which the peso floats is between 1110 pesos and 1276 pesos to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent hesitancy towards \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  casts doubts on whether the Bank will enter (the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market) before the exchange rate reaches the upper bound of the band," the report added. \par \par \uc2  In addition to violence staged by leftist guerillas, another threat hangs over Colombia, the report said. \par \par \uc2  A bomb discovered last week in Medellin was claimed by a group called the "extraditables". That group has promised more bombs to come in response to recent moves in Congress to end Colombia's six-year-old ban on extradition. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT  09-09-97 \par \par \uc2  1830GMT \par \par \uc2  1802 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011006dt9900co7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
