\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso Slides Amid  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 1996\par 23:06\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso slid marginally against the dollar Friday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars to keep the exchange rate above the floor of the exchange band, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's weighted exchange rate rose to 1,001.45, from 1,001.1 pesos on Thursday, with intraday trading fluctuating between 1,001.45 pesos and 1,001.47 pesos to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume was about $80 million, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The market was very stable with only minor variations in trading of about two (Colombian) cents," one trader said. The peso is divided into 100 cents. \par \par \uc2  The trader said that the market's tendency is for the peso to strengthen as exporters and investors buy pesos. The demand for the dollar, meanwhile, remains weak. \par \par \uc2  As a result, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $25 million Friday to force the exchange rate to remain at the level of the floor set for trading. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows the peso to fluctuate freely within preset maximum and minimum values that allow the peso to fall gradually against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The floor on Friday was 1,001.45 pesos, from 1,001.1 pesos on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  By policy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market or how many dollars it buys or sells, but traders estimated that it bought about $25 million on Friday - nearly one third of the total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market - to force the peso to slide to the floor set for Friday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso has fallen about 1.46% against the dollar so far this year.\par    -Keefe Borden\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 20-12-96\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2206GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1068 1802 1845 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011013dsck00n7e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
