\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso Slides Vs. Dollar As  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 1996\par 22:47\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso slid against the dollar Tuesday amid agressive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said, noting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold pesos to keep the dollar within the exchange bands. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's weighted exchange rate rose to 1,000.41 pesos, from 1,000.07 pesos on Monday, with intraday trading fluctuating between 1,000.40 pesos and 1,000.44 pesos to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume was $145 million. \par \par \uc2  "The overall market didn't change much. The peso continues to move along the floor of the exchange band," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows the peso to float freely within preset exchange boundaries, whose midpoint allows for a 13.6% devaluation against the dollar in 1996. \par \par \uc2  The floor of the exchange band, which was set at 1,000.41 on Tuesday, is 7% below the midpoint. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys dollars when the exchange rate hits the floor. On Tuesday, it purchased about $45 million, about a third of the total market for the day. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the peso was helped by coffee, sugar, and oil exports as well as by the Colombian treasury, which brought in capital it had borrowed on foreign debt markets. \par \par \uc2  The demand for the peso, meanwhile, remains weak. \par \par \uc2  With many market participants trying to sell dollars and few trying to buy them, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in Tuesday's markets to keep the peso above the floor, which will rise to 1,000.76 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso has fallen about 1.3% against the dollar so far this year.\par    -Keefe Borden\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 17-12-96\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2147GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1068 1802 1845 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011013dsch00mlc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
