\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso Slides As  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 1996\par 22:45\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--The Colombian peso slid against the dollar Monday amid stable trading as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars to keep the exchange rate above the floor it set for trading, sources said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's weighted exchange rate rose to 1,000.07 pesos, from 999.02 on Friday, with intraday trading fluctuating between 1,000.06 pesos and 1,000.15 pesos to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume was $77 million, a trader said. \par \par \uc2  "The truth is, it was a market with very little volatility," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  The trader said the peso continues to be boosted by coffee and oil exports and by private companies which have borrowed on international debt markets. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars to keep the exchange rate within the preset exchange band, whose floor was 999.03 pesos on Friday and 1,000.06 pesos on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Practically all of the trading occurred on or near the floor of the exchange band," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows the dollar to trade freely within a pre-set exchange band whose midpoint allows for a 13.6% devaluation against the dollar in 1996. The floor is 7% below the midpoint. \par \par \uc2  For most of last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased dollars to keep the peso at least at the level of the floor. Traders said that tendency continued on Monday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought an estimated $9 million to force the peso to slide against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The peso is expected to continue to slide against the dollar on Tuesday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise the floor to 1,000.41 pesos. The dollar was trading at 1,000.42 pesos on the "next day" market, which reflects trades made late one day but not executed until the following day. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso has fallen about 1.3% against the dollar so far this year.\par    -Keefe Borden\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 16-12-96\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2145GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1068 1802 1845 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011013dscg00mex\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
