\par\par \b \uc2  Colombia Peso -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Seen Buying About $35 Mln \b0\par\par\uc2 219 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 1996\par 22:28\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  But overall, the peso slipped Tuesday as the Bank of the Republic, Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , aggressively purchased dollars after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  touched the floor of the exchange band, which was set at 997.99 pesos Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy specifies that it won't acknowledge when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. But one trader Tuesday estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $35 million to force the peso to slide against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows the dollar to float freely between pre-set minimum and maximum values. The midpoint of the exchange band allows for a 13.6% nominal devaluation against the dollar in 1996. The floor and ceiling are 7% below and above the midpoint. \par \par \uc2  As of 2300 GMT, no trades had been made on Tuesday's "next day" market, which reflects transactions made one day but not executed until the next trading day. \par \par \uc2  The peso is expected to slide against the dollar again Wednesday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise the floor of the exchange band to 998.33 pesos. \par \par \uc2  The peso has fallen about 1.1% against the dollar so far this year. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 10-12-96 \par \par \uc2  2128GMT \par \par \uc2  1068 1802 1845 \par \par \uc2 Dokum