\par\par \b \uc2  Colombia's net foreign reserves at year high. \b0\par\par\uc2 202 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, Dec 2 (Reuter) - Colombia's net foreign reserves stood at $8.32 billion as of November 15, the most recent date for which officials figures are available, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The reserve figure was the highest reported by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or Banco de la Republica, since Oct 28 of last year when net reserves stood at $8.38 billion. \par \par \uc2  A recent increase in foreign investment flows, coupled with a surge in dollar-denominated loans and flagging demand for U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  have contributed to the increase in the country's overall foreign reserves. \par \par \uc2  The bank has been forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by buying dollars in recent weeks to halt the peso's strengthening against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The peso, which was trading at more than 1,070 to the dollar in June, closed at 994.19 Friday.  Its rise has put a strain on exporters, who have seen their revenues in real peso terms shrink steadily in recent months despite an increase in production costs stemming from inflation totalling 20.76 percent so far this year. \par \par \uc2  -- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019dsc202o87\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
