\par\par \b \uc2  Colombia Peso Closes Steady Vs Dlr As  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Buys \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 1996\par 22:41\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--The Colombia peso closed steady against the dollar Friday as supply and demand for dollars balanced each other out, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's weighted exchange rate rose marginally to 994.8 pesos, from 994.76 pesos on Thursday, with intraday trading fluctuating between 994.19 pesos and 997 pesos to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume was $132 million in 279 separate transactions, a trader said. \par \par \uc2  The peso began to weaken against the dollar early Friday as banks speculated that it would weaken in the coming days. \par \par \uc2  By mid-morning, however, the peso began to regain some of the ground it lost against the dollar as coffee and petroleum exporters repatriated dollar earnings. \par \par \uc2  In addition, the U.S. embassy reportedly bought between $4 million and $5 million in pesos from several banks, boosting the strength of the peso. \par \par \uc2  The peso closed the session on the floor of the exchange band, which was set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 994.19 pesos on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $15 million to halt the peso's strengthening trend. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't reveal on a daily basis how much it spends \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The peso is expected to slide against the dollar on Monday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will adjust the floor to 995.22 pesos to the dollar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso has fallen about 0.8% against the dollar so far this year.\par    -Keefe Borden\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 29-11-96\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2141GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1068 1802 1845 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011013dsbt00nql\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
