\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso Strengthens Despite Reported  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 1996\par 23:17\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso gained against the dollar Wednesday despite reports of "aggressive" \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weigh it down, traders reported. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's weighted exchange rate fell to 1,003.31 pesos, from 1,007.35 pesos on Tuesday, with intraday trading fluctuating between 1,002.8 pesos and 1,004.7 pesos to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume was $111 million in 281 separate transactions, a trader said. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimated that the Bank of the Republic, Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , purchased between $20 and $25 million to slow the peso's upvaluation. Had the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso would have strengthened to around 1,000 to the dollar on Wednesday, he said. \par \par \uc2  "It (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) was buying pretty aggressively," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  By policy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't acknowledge when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but a recent statement acknowledged that it had purchased $78 million in recent weeks to slow the peso's upvaluation. \par \par \uc2  A trader at a major bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was flush with dollars despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts. Coffee exporters and foreign investors, particularly in oil and telecommunications sold an unreported quantity of dollars. \par \par \uc2  The peso's growing strength, however, didn't spark a reaction from companies or banks to buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but one trader said he believed many banks were waiting for the peso to hit the psychological barrier of 1,000 pesos to the dollar before buying pesos. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 30-10-96 \par \par \uc2  2217GMT \par \par \uc2  1068 1802 1845 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011013dsau00i2s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
