\par\par \b \uc2  Colombia Peso Gains Vs. Dlr Amid Heavy Dlr Supply \b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 1996\par 00:01\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--The Colombia peso strengthened against the dollar Tuesday amid a plentiful supply of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's weighted exchange rate declined to 1,017.55 pesos from 1,018.37 pesos on Monday. The exchange rate fluctuated between 1,016.50 pesos and 1,018.90 pesos to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The volume of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was $108 million in 299 separate transactions. \par \par \uc2  "This week the market opened with a large supply of dollars amid speculative pressures," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  Expectations last week that \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Banco de la Republica, would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stop the peso's recent gains against the dollar, had caused the peso to decline slightly, the trader added. However, the peso began to gain against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided not to take expected drastic measures to bolster the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Trading on the "next day" market - transactions made late Tuesday but not carried out until Wednesday - was light, with $3 million trading hands at an average rate of 1,017.50 pesos. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso has fallen about 3.0% against the dollar so far this year.\par    -Guillermo Tovar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 22-10-96\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2201GMT\par \f28 \