\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso Slides Vs. Dollar On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Hopes \b0\par\par\uc2 254 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 1996\par 00:15\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso weakened against the dollar Monday amid expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take measures to slow the peso's recent strengthening, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's weighted exchange rate rose to 1,018.37 pesos, from 1,015.36 pesos on Friday. The peso's weakest exchange rate on Monday was 1,019.85 pesos to the dollar, while its strongest exchange rate was 1,014.9 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The volume of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was $118 million in 317 separate transactions, about average by the standards of recent weeks, a trader said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued a statement on Friday in which it acknowledged buying a total of $78 million recently to slow the peso's recent upvaluation. \par \par \uc2  It also stated that it would buy more dollars as it considered necessary in the coming weeks to slow the peso's recent strengthening. The peso has gained about 4% on the dollar since July, boosted by exports and a weak demand for the dollar. \par \par \uc2  A trader at a major Colombian bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement prompted the peso to slide when the market first opened, but that it began to regain some of its lost ground when coffee exporters and investors in the petroleum sector sold dollars for pesos. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso has fallen about 3.1% against the dollar so far this year.\par    -Keefe Borden\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (EN