\par\par \b \uc2  Colombian government seeks to weaken buoyant peso. \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, Aug 13 (Reuter) - Finance Minister Jose Antonio Ocampo said the government was studying a number of measures aimed at weakening Colombia's buoyant peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help make the country's exports more competitive abroad. \par \par \uc2  "It's not a matter of triggering an excessive devaluation, but we don't want an execessive appreciation either," Ocampo told reporters. \par \par \uc2  "Stopping the appreciation is a priority," he added. \par \par \uc2  The peso, which was trading at 1,070 in late June, has risen steadily in recent weeks as a flood of dollars from foreign oil sales entered the country. \par \par \uc2  Dealers on the country's interbank market have also attributed the rise of the peso, which closed at a six-month high of 1,030.20 Monday, to dollar sales by banks and a drop in demand for U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the corporate sector. \par \par \uc2  Ocampo did not spell out what measures the government might take to halt the peso's meteoric rise. \par \par \uc2  But he said it had urged \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the interbank market by buying dollars and undercutting the peso. \par \par \uc2  President Ernesto Samper urged the bank in a speech last week to push down its floating exchange rate band in a bid to weaken the peso and shore up the export sector. \par \par \uc2  But the bank, which likes a strong peso as a shield against inflation, has insisted that the exchange rate band will not be altered. It currently stands at 957.64 to 1,101.81 pesos to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The band is set daily according to a slated pace of depreciation and the peso is currently in the middle of the band. Dealers see no problem in maintaining the current band. \par \par \uc2  The government had forecast a 13.6 percent devaluation of the peso this year. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost only 5.3 percent of its value against the dollar so far. \par \par \uc2  -- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds8d04h5e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
