\par\par \b \uc2  Colombian peso ends down on U.S. drug report. \b0\par\par\uc2 191 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, March 1 (Reuter) - Colombia's peso ended down 55 centavos at 1,049.90 to the dollar -- on the floor of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official exchange rate band, interbank traders said. \par \par \uc2  It was the 10th consecutive session in which the peso closed lower on spiraling political uncertainty in Colombia. \par \par \uc2  Traders noted that the market closed minutes before it was announced in Washington that the United States was dropping Colombia from a list of favored nations that cooperate in the international anti-drug fight. \par \par \uc2  But several said the move had already been discounted. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in early trade, selling up to $2 million to stabilize the peso, traders said. But they said it was generally firmer than in previous sessions this week when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold tens of millions of dollars to prop up the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Though the peso could come under a new speculative assault next week, traders and market analysts say \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has ample reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and inject stability into the market. \par \par \uc2  --Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds3100v31\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
