\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso Resumes Slide As Central Banks  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 187 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 1996\par 23:07\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOGOTA (DJ-EMR)--The Colombian political crisis caused the peso to slide against the dollar Monday despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up its value, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened at 1,027.8 pesos and closed at 1,027.99 pesos, the minimum exchange rate set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for trading on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent an estimated $12 million to $15 million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the peso's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, one trader said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's total volume Monday was $92 million. \par \par \uc2  The peso continued to slide despite a light jump in overnight lending rates, which normally make savings more attractive in pesos, the trader said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight lending rates fluctuated between 23% and 24% Monday, compared with 19% on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The trader said that the Colombian political crisis continues to undermine confidence in the peso. \par \par \uc2  President Ernesto Samper's administration has been shaken by renewed allegations that he knowingly received millions of dollars in contributions from the Cali drug cartel. \par \par \uc2  --Keefe Borden \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 01-29-96 \par \par \uc2  1707EST \par \par \uc2  1802 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011013ds1t001ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\