\par\par \b \uc2  Colombia peso ends down at 1,001.55. \b0\par\par\uc2 204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, Nov 24 (Reuter) - Colombia's peso slipped 1.25 against the dollar in subdued interbank trading to end the week at 1,001.55, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said exporters changing U.S. dollar earnings into pesos boosted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an intraday high of 999.30 early in the session -- back above the 1,000-to-one psychological barrier broken last week. But dollar buying by banks pushed it steadily lower ahead of the close. \par \par \uc2  Most dealers and economic analysts expect the peso, which has already lost more than 20 pct this year, to continue losing ground until Colombia's political crisis has been resolved. \par \par \uc2  The crisis, and prevailing uncertainty in Colombia, stems from an investigation into charges that President Samper's 1994 election campaign was partly financed by drug lords. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the interbank market repeatedly in recent weeks to keep the peso within its 15- pct trading band. The crawling peg devaluation benefitted exporters, however, and helped fuel stronger-than-expected economic growth in the third quarter. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported 317 \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday for a total of $124.2 million. \par \par \uc2  --Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drbo01ea3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
