\par\par \b \uc2  Colombian peso posts gains against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, Aug 28 (Reuter) - Colombia's peso, battered over the past week by the country's deepening political crisis, strengthened against the dollar on Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly to shore it up. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Guillermo Perry, meanwhile, said the government was studying measures to increase the supply of greenbacks in Colombia and vowed the current exchange band would remain in place. \par \par \uc2  "The phenomenon that we're seeing is purely a product of speculation," Perry told reporters, referring to the peso's recent drop against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The peso's fall, triggered at least in part by political uncertainty stemming from allegations of drug-related contributions to President Ernesto Samper's 1994 campaign, has put a drain on \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop it. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  all morning," one dealer said of Monday's session, which ended with the dollar down 3.01 pesos on the interbank market at 970.50, off its intraday low of 974. The dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped selling dollars before midday, but the market "tended to stabilize" quickly after the bank's selling spree. \par \par \uc2  In his remarks to reporters, Perry did not specify the measures the government might take to increase the supply of dollars in Colombia. \par \par \uc2  But economic analysts say that, in addition to political uncertainty, and the resulting flight to quality into U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the flow of dollars into Colombia has ebbed as a result of the recent crackdown on the Cali drug cartel and the arrests of all, but one of its top leaders. \par \par \uc2  Prior to the crackdown, the cartel controlled most of the cocaine smuggled into the United States and was a major source of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -- Tom Brown, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr8s04knm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
